HST Office: the remaining error values of HST Sheets follow the leading spreadsheet application
(measured with its 2021 version on 2026-11-13), and formula results never depend on a GPU driver.

- sc calcconfig.cxx, tpcalc.cxx: formulas are never computed by the OpenCL kernels. They report
  errors with their own codes (#VALUE! where the interpreter gives #NUM! since
  hst-sheets-num-errors.patch, and other differences), so a result would depend on the graphics
  driver. The "Allow use of OpenCL" box of the Sheets options is disabled; the explicit test override
  SC_FORCE_CALCULATION=opencl still runs the kernels.
- sc interpr3.cxx: PROB checks only that the probabilities add up to 1 (#NUM! otherwise), as the
  leading application does; single probabilities outside [0;1] are not an error there.
- sc interpr2.cxx: NETWORKDAYS.INTL / WORKDAY.INTL with an invalid weekend number give #NUM!; an
  invalid weekend string stays #VALUE!.
- sc interpr1.cxx: WRAPROWS / WRAPCOLS with a wrap count below 1 give #NUM! (a negative count no longer
  wraps around to a huge size).
- scaddins analysishelper, sc addincol.cxx: CONVERT with an unknown unit or units of different kinds
  gives #N/A (the add-in throws a RuntimeException "#N/A", which the add-in call maps to #N/A).
- scaddins pricing.cxx: an unknown option word (put/call, in/out, ...) or a non-numeric strike of the
  OPT_* functions is #VALUE! (wrong kind of value), numbers outside the model stay #NUM!. These
  functions have no counterpart in the leading application.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_sheets_error_parity.py, tests/runtime/check-sheets-excel-formula-conventions.py.
